        question: "Why are cattle alleys curved instead of straight?",
        answer: "Because cattle follow curves calmly. A curved alley with solid sides lets each animal see a couple of head ahead without seeing the chute or a dead end, so they keep walking instead of balking. Straight alleys work for pen-to-pen moves, but the working alley to the chute is curved by design — it is cattle psychology built into steel.",
